# ─── Mobile build-time environment variables ──────────────────────────────────
# Copy to .env (gitignored) and fill in values, OR export before running Metro.
#
# These are inlined at bundle time by babel-plugin-transform-inline-environment-variables.
# Changes require a Metro cache reset:  pnpm --filter @g88/mobile start:reset
#
# Usage:
#   cp apps/mobile/.env.example apps/mobile/.env
#   # edit .env, then:
#   pnpm --filter @g88/mobile android
#
# Switching between emulator and a physical device? Keep two local presets
# (.env.emulator / .env.device, both gitignored) and swap the active .env with:
#   pnpm --filter @g88/mobile env:emulator   # then: ... start:reset
#   pnpm --filter @g88/mobile env:device     # edit its API_HOST first
# This avoids a stale API_HOST (e.g. localhost) breaking emulator login.

# ─── Dev API host ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave UNSET for emulator/simulator — config.ts defaults per platform:
#   Android emulator → 10.0.2.2  (AVD loopback to host machine)
#   iOS simulator    → localhost
# Set explicitly only for a physical device:
#   Android USB      → localhost  (requires: adb reverse tcp:3001 tcp:3001)
#   Android Wi-Fi    → your machine's LAN IP (e.g. 192.168.1.42)
#   Prod backend     → g88-api.onrender.com  (https inferred)
# API_HOST=192.168.1.42

# ─── Google Sign-In ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OAuth 2.0 Web Client ID from Google Cloud Console.
# Must match the GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID env var on the backend.
# GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=1234567890-xxxx.apps.googleusercontent.com

# ─── Sentry (project g88/g88) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Public DSN — safe to ship in the client. Leave empty to disable Sentry entirely.
# CI android-apk injects secrets.SENTRY_DSN at bundle time.
SENTRY_DSN=https://d650757e8196e9741e68d09af8ba826d@o4511452296970240.ingest.de.sentry.io/4511477529051216
#
# Optional release identity (defaults: com.g88@0.1.0+0 locally).
# CI sets these to match the APK versionCode so source-map uploads can attach.
# SENTRY_RELEASE=com.g88@0.1.0+42
# SENTRY_DIST=42
#
# Native / source-map upload (NOT inlined into the app — CI / local release builds only):
#   Create a Sentry auth token (org:read, project:releases, project:write) and store as
#   GitHub secret SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN. Required after running:
#     npx @sentry/wizard@latest -i reactNative
#   which wires Xcode + Gradle upload hooks. Token must never be committed.
